{"_meta":{"system":"mutation_visuals","version":"1.0.0","schema":"extended-1","owner_task":"T04","status":"active","notes":"What each mutation looks like, keyed by mutation id. A mutation definition carries behaviour; this file carries appearance, so adding a mutation means adding one style here and no renderer change. Styles are looked up by id first and by ordinal (declaration order, 1..N) second, which is what a rival plant ships. `target` names the organs the style touches (foliage = leaf and cotyledon, woody = root, stem, branch, trunk, vine, seed = the seed coat, bloom = flower and spore sac, whole = every organ), so a mutation never paints an organ its name does not promise. `pattern` picks a procedural figure and `pattern_scale` sizes it. Colours are linear multipliers on the organ texture, not absolute colours: the plant still reads as a plant, and stacked mutations multiply, so `caps` bounds what any stack may reach."},"values":{"caps":{"type":"object","value":{"min_tint":0.55,"max_tint":1.35,"max_tint_strength":0.9,"max_variegation":0.8,"max_glow":0.95,"max_bark_thickness":1.6,"max_bark_darken":0.45,"max_spines":1,"level_visual_gain":0.35},"notes":"Ceilings for a composed look. Tints multiply across stacked mutations and would blow a channel out without a clamp, and bark thickness would stack without bound. level_visual_gain amplifies a style by this share per level above the first, so a levelled mutation is visibly stronger."},"targets":{"type":"object","value":{"foliage":["leaf","cotyledon"],"woody":["root","stem","branch","trunk","vine"],"seed":["seed"],"bloom":["flower","spore_sac"],"whole":[]},"notes":"Organ families a style target covers. `whole` means every organ and is the fallback for a mutation that is about the organism, not one organ."},"styles":{"type":"object","value":{"bioluminescent_lamina":{"target":"foliage","pattern":"glow","pattern_scale":1,"tint":[1.02,1.04,1],"tint_strength":0.2,"variegation":0,"variegation_color":[1,1,1],"glow":0.55